## Method and reasoning
Keep a max-heap for the lower half and a min-heap for the upper half. Keep the lower heap equal in size or one larger. Insert according to the lower maximum and rebalance by moving a boundary element. The lower maximum is the median, including on even-sized prefixes.

## Walk through the sample
After inserting 5 and 0, the halves are [0] and [5], giving lower median 0. With a third value 5, the lower half must contain two elements; its maximum becomes 5.

## Complexity
Time O(n log n), space O(n).

## Reference implementation
~~~
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);
    int n;
    cin >> n;
    priority_queue<int> low;
    priority_queue<int, vector<int>, greater<int>> high;
    while (n--) {
        int x;
        cin >> x;
        if (low.empty() || x <= low.top())
            low.push(x);
        else
            high.push(x);
        if (low.size() > high.size() + 1) {
            high.push(low.top());
            low.pop();
        }
        if (high.size() > low.size()) {
            low.push(high.top());
            high.pop();
        }
        cout << low.top() << '\n';
    }
}
